Correct. Uniformity is the enemy of drama, and stars are nothing if not dramatic. Well spotted.
Why do stars represent a new level of complexity in the Universe?
They have solid cores
Oh, come on! Stars aren’t solid. They’re plasmatic temper tantrums held together by gravity. Try again before our star flares out.
They have a strong gravitational pull
Incorrect. While technically true, this isn’t why stars added complexity. Try again before the Universe stops expanding.
They generate energy through nuclear fusion
Yes. Fusion—it’s not just for mediocre restaurant concepts. It can also liven up your Universe.
